# --- Python ---
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Local configuration (never committed) ---
config.local.json

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Run log (not a product) ---
# Carries per-step timings and differs on every run; tracking it would leave
# git status permanently dirty.
dist/pipeline_report.txt

# --- Patch notes (travel with a patch ZIP, never into the repository) ---
PATCH-README.md

# --- Note ---
# docs/ and dist/ are NOT ignored, unlike the usual Python template: docs/ is
# what GitHub Pages serves, dist/ holds the citable products (graph, GeoJSON,
# BibTeX). data/raw/ is not ignored either: the harvest cache is committed so
# that every build after S3 runs offline (PRIMER A3).

# --- Web products before they reach docs/ (S6) ---
# Written by cite/rdf/map in the layout of docs/ and copied in by the site step.
# docs/ is the published copy; tracking this one too would double every file.
data/derived/web/

# --- Step cache (S8b) ---
# Fingerprints of the last rdf/validate run, so an unchanged run can skip them.
# Machine-local by nature; a fresh clone just builds everything once.
data/derived/cache/
PATCH-README.md